    "feedback-opening": {
      "id": "feedback-opening",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A completed worker leaves attempt evidence that later workers can reuse. When worker summarization is enabled, the summary job reads the transcript and checkpoint digest, validates the narrative, stores attempt records, and queues a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run_closed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " task. The librarian then researches whether those results support new or revised claims."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "feedback-handoff-h": {
      "id": "feedback-handoff-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "From Attempt to Knowledge"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "feedback-steps": {
      "id": "feedback-steps",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "Capture the completed attempt",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "The summary job writes worker_run, submission, and run_narrative records. Scores and integration outcomes come from deterministic run state; the model supplies narrative fields."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Queue librarian review",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Advance the attempt watermark and enqueue a run_closed index_task. The task remains pending until an enabled consumer or manual drain claims it."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Research the affected subjects",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Read the run, scored submissions, current records, and supporting source material. A failed hypothesis remains attempt history; an outcome alone is not a fact."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Validate and apply supported changes",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Check subjects, scope, and citations. Accepted fact writes replace their evidence rows together. Cite the run or submission with an attempt:// locator."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Record coverage and drift results",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Stamp covered subjects and complete the task. Passes with code drift retry once; unresolved drift after the retry completes with a recorded warning."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "feedback-integration-h": {
      "id": "feedback-integration-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Integration Outcomes"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "feedback-integration": {
      "id": "feedback-integration",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A useful attempt can still conflict during integration. The run-loop records "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integration_detail",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " from run state. The next worker can inspect the attempt and conflict paths instead of repeating its research. Integration status and compiler scores remain attempt history; the librarian separately evaluates semantic claims."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "feedback-citations-h": {
      "id": "feedback-citations-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "What the Librarian Can Learn"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "feedback-citations": {
      "id": "feedback-citations",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The librarian reads structured attempt history first and can corroborate claims through code, PRs, Discord, or the wiki. Supported behavior belongs in cited facts. A recurring technique may support a curated pattern. Workers can also search these sources; the librarian owns proposing semantic updates through the apply layer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
